From 08ba5b75a24df34df4b983af66c90378a6e617fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SovereignOS Build <build@sovereignos.local>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:15:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 89/89] sovereignos: re-evaluate the user-switcher StateFlow on
 keyguard transitions

UserRepositoryImpl._userSwitcherSettings is a StateFlow built from
globalSettings.observerFlow() over three Settings.Global keys
(SETTING_SIMPLE_USER_SWITCHER, ADD_USERS_WHEN_LOCKED,
USER_SWITCHER_ENABLED). Its getSettings() mapper calls
manager.isUserSwitcherEnabled(), which is itself live and
keyguard-state-aware (it additionally hides the switcher for a Duress
Unlock decoy session without touching the device-wide setting) -- but
the StateFlow's cached value only refreshes when one of those three
keys changes via ContentObserver. A keyguard showing-state transition
with no Settings.Global write leaves the cached value stale until some
unrelated settings write happens to refresh it.

Merge KeyguardRepository.isKeyguardShowing into the StateFlow's
upstream alongside the existing observerFlow(), so a keyguard
transition re-evaluates getSettings() even when none of the three
settings keys changed. KeyguardRepository is already a sibling
dependency of UserTracker inside KeyguardRepositoryImpl and introduces
no circular dependency with UserRepository.
---
 .../data/repository/UserRepositoryImplTest.kt | 22 ++++++++++++++++
 .../data/repository/UserRepositoryImpl.kt     | 26 +++++++++++++------
 2 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/multivalentTests/src/com/android/systemui/user/data/repository/UserRepositoryImplTest.kt b/packages/SystemUI/multivalentTests/src/com/android/systemui/user/data/repository/UserRepositoryImplTest.kt
